Description: 4k Intro for Linux, released in 2011
 Stochastic Lens Simulator is a 4k intro by Gzrrplox, released at
 Instanssi 2011. It is a first step towards a realtime stochastic
 micropolygon rasterizer: geometry is sampled at random time and lens
 coordinates many times per pixel, which gives motion blur and depth of
 field. Sound is also generated on the GPU.
 .
 This package is built from the source code shipped with the intro, and
 requires an OpenGL 3.2 driver with geometry shader support.
